  "notes": "Yamamoto-first discovery pass under the current durable repository rubric. docs/PRIORITIES.md, docs/EDITORIAL.md, docs/DOMAINS.md, and radar/inbox/README.md were reread before discovery and grading. Current Tsuyoshi Yamamoto sources were checked first, including Jazz House ALFIE, BODY&SOUL, current schedule traces, Space M&A-related searches, and credible Japanese jazz sources; no additional unrecorded Yamamoto appearance with a distinct event-specific admission reason was verified in this pass. Shun Ishiwaka Trio featuring Yusei Takahashi and Marty Holoubek with guest Tomoaki Baba clears RADAR admission on performance-specific grounds: Okegawa is the final published date of the quartet's first hall tour around Mabui, an all-Ishiwaka-composition project whose four players share Terumasa Hino-group lineage and whose instrumentation combines drums, piano/electric piano and electronics, bass, and tenor saxophone. Priority was assigned only after admission. A+ is sufficient: this is an unusually strong new-generation Japanese jazz project and a meaningful tour-closing Kanto date worth making room for, but it is one stop in a six-city tour rather than a farewell, one-off premiere, or otherwise scarce enough to justify S. The proposed A+ is consistent with the current editorial shape of a broad A base, narrower A+, and rare S/S+ tiers. Batch distribution: A 0, A+ 1, S 0, S+ 0.",
